{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBzc2wpMV9nyq9kAASkQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The O3 frontend formats dates in one place, `formatDate` in the esm-utils package of `openmrs-esm-core`. It reads the current locale, prints \"Today\" for the current day, and appends the time when needed.\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. **Locale:** `formatDate` calls `getLocale()` unless the caller passes `options.locale`. `getLocale()` reads `window.i18next.language`, normalises it to a BCP 47 tag, and maps `ht` to `fr-HT` (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/get-locale.ts:7-18`).\n2. **Defaults:** `mode: 'standard'`, `time: 'for today'`, `day`/`month`/`year` on, and `noToday: false`. For the Amharic (`am`) locale, `noToday` defaults to `true`, so no \"Today\" is produced there (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts:208-215` and `:310-314`).\n3. **\"Today\":** `dayjs(date).isToday()` is checked. If the date is today and `noToday` is false, it uses `Intl.RelativeTimeFormat(locale, { numeric: 'auto' })` with `format(0, 'day')`, which yields the word in the locale's language, and capitalises its first letter (`date-util.ts:327-332`).\n4. **Other dates:** `Intl.DateTimeFormat` is used with `year: 'numeric'`, `month: 'short'`, and `day: '2-digit'`. English uses `en-GB` so the output is day-first. For `en` and `am` in `standard` mode, spaces become hyphens. `wide` mode uses \" — \" separators. The Ethiopic calendar's era is stripped (`date-util.ts:334-364`).\n5. **Time:** appended as `, ${formatTime(date)}` when `time === true`, or when the date is today and `time` is `'for today'`. `formatTime` uses `toLocaleTimeString` with 2-digit hour and minute (`date-util.ts:368-401`).\n6. **Helpers:** `formatDatetime` calls `formatDate` with `time: true` (`date-util.ts:416-418`). `formatPartialDate` handles partial strings such as \"2000-01\" by parsing them and passing the result to `formatDate` (`date-util.ts:241-280`).\n\n**Documentation**\n\nThe public docs are generated from the same JSDoc. `formatDate.md` describes the defaults, the \"Today\" behaviour, and the `noToday: true` opt-out (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/formatDate.md:1-46`). `formatDatetime.md` covers the datetime variant, and `API.md` links both.\n\n**Tests**\n\n`date-util.test.ts` checks the \"Today\" output in several locales, for example `Today, 03:22 PM` in English and `Сегодня, 15:22` in Russian (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.test.ts:54-66`).\n\nI did not search the patient chart repository for consumers of these helpers, and I did not run the tests.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 306, \"endLine\": 372},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 208, \"endLine\": 215},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 180, \"endLine\": 206},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 217, \"endLine\": 239},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 282, \"endLine\": 305},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 374, \"endLine\": 387},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 389, \"endLine\": 401},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 403, \"endLine\": 418},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts\", \"startLine\": 241, \"endLine\": 280},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/get-locale.ts\", \"startLine\": 3, \"endLine\